  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Adds Sage-compatible Matrix.set_row, set_column, and set_block for packed dense GF(p) matrices. Values are coerced before mutation, then one source-transparent native call commits the checked row, column, or block transactionally. Odd-prime storage copies packed UInt64Buffer data directly; GF(2) traverses borrowed M4RI resources without exporting either matrix. Native-disabled execution uses the same typed source. On the controlled 512x512 workload, row and column batches take about 1-2 ms instead of 12-20 ms, while 96x96 blocks take about 0.08-1.3 ms instead of 329-355 ms.",
    "risks": [
      "Only the compiler-owned small-prime and M4RI representations implement these public batch methods; other base rings still report the explicit NotImplementedError.",
      "Linux x64 is validated locally; the source-transparent kernels and portable fallbacks still depend on normal macOS arm64, Linux arm64, and Windows x64 CI coverage."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Extend the same public batch API to generated exact ZZ and QQ matrix resources when those operations are prioritized.",
      "Consider compiler-owned packed prime-field vectors so already-canonical vector inputs can avoid the remaining host-side coercion scan."
    ]
  }
